# Setting a 1% Stop Loss in MQL5 (MetaTrader 5)

To programmatically set a stop loss that represents 1% of your trading balance in MQL5, you'll need to calculate the appropriate price level based on your account balance and the current market price. Here's how to do it:

## Basic Implementation

```mql5
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Function to calculate 1% stop loss level                         |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
double CalculateStopLossPrice(ENUM_TRADE_REQUEST_ACTIONS action, double current_price)
{
   double balance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
   double risk_amount = balance * 0.01; // 1% of balance

   // Get symbol info
   string symbol = Symbol();
   double point = SymbolInfoDouble(symbol, SYMBOL_POINT);
   double tick_value = SymbolInfoDouble(symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
   double lot_size = SymbolInfoDouble(symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_CONTRACT_SIZE);

   // Calculate lot size based on risk (1% of balance)
   double lot = NormalizeDouble(risk_amount / (tick_value * lot_size * 10), 2); // 10 pips stop

   // Calculate stop loss price
   double sl_points = (risk_amount / (lot * tick_value * lot_size)) / point;
   double sl_price;

   if(action == TRADE_ACTION_BUY)
      sl_price = current_price - (sl_points * point);
   else // TRADE_ACTION_SELL
      sl_price = current_price + (sl_points * point);

   return sl_price;
}
```

## Complete Order Placement Example

Here's how to use it when placing an order:

```mql5
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Script program start function                                    |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void OnStart()
{
   // Get current price
   MqlTick last_tick;
   if(!SymbolInfoTick(_Symbol, last_tick))
   {
      Print("Failed to get tick data");
      return;
   }

   double current_price = (last_tick.ask + last_tick.bid) / 2;

   // Calculate stop loss price
   double sl_price = CalculateStopLossPrice(TRADE_ACTION_BUY, current_price);

   // Prepare request
   MqlTradeRequest request = {0};
   request.action = TRADE_ACTION_DEAL;
   request.symbol = _Symbol;
   request.volume = 0.1; // You might want to calculate this based on your risk
   request.type = ORDER_TYPE_BUY;
   request.price = last_tick.ask;
   request.sl = sl_price;
   request.tp = 0; // No take profit
   request.deviation = 5;
   request.magic = 12345;
   request.comment = "1% risk trade";
   request.type_filling = ORDER_FILLING_FOK;

   // Send request
   if(!OrderSend(request))
   {
      Print("OrderSend failed, error: ", GetLastError());
      return;
   }

   Print("Order placed successfully with 1% stop loss");
}
```

## Alternative Simplified Version

If you prefer a simpler approach that doesn't calculate position size:

```mql5
